      "id": 1,
      "text": "Plankinton was founded in 1879 as a railroad stop when the Milwaukee Railroad line pushed westward across the Dakota Territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wikixm.com/us/sd/plankinton/overview"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Plankinton serves as the county seat of Aurora County and is colloquially known as Plank.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plankinton%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Aurora County Courthouse, built in 1881, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wikixm.com/us/sd/plankinton/overview"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Sweep Hotel in Plankinton has been named to the National Register of Historic Places.",
